## Context
DESIGN.md §4 PR-1, honoring R23. Verified defect at edf2748: createSchema
re-stamps SCHEMA_VERSION via INSERT OR REPLACE (sqlite-index.ts:26,153) before
loadMeta ever reads it — the stamp is written and read nowhere, so a downgrade
destroys the evidence of skew at the moment it matters. The PR: read
meta.schemaVersion before any DDL or write; unknown/newer -> sideline the file
(.incompatible-<ts>, never delete), fresh build, one notice. Failing test: open
a fixture stamped schemaVersion=99, assert it is not re-stamped and is
sidelined. Form: PR, no issue (contained defect + failing test — merged twice
per SYNC.md). #20 merged 2026-08-27; re-verify the evidence at v1.8.0 first —
`2f453d6` moved this file family (store-faults.ts, repair.ts, the narrowed
catches).

## Exit criteria
- [x] failing test demonstrates the re-stamp on a version-99 fixture (5 of 7 fail on unpatched v1.8.0 main)
- [x] read-before-write + sideline protocol in the PR, tests green on his tree (fd51659: 733/7, typecheck+lint clean)
- [x] PR opened upstream 2026-08-28 as #25 — open, CI green; record the outcome here when it lands
